module v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_admission

import v2.std.collection { List }
import v2.std.logic { Bool }
import gunbc.floor_cost_distribution {
  ClaimCostReading, ObservedCpuReading, RightCensoredCpuReading, CpuLowerBoundWithoutCeiling,
}
import std.measure { Millisecond, millisecond, millisecond_count, EvalStepCount, eval_step_count }

// ROSTER ADMISSION BY CONSTRUCTION FOR `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt`.
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT INSIDE THAT MODULE. `required_floor` already imports `floor_cost_debt` for
// membership. Importing `ClaimCostReading` there would pull `gunbc.floor_cost_distribution`
// into every required-floor compile — a second copy of a large analysis module on the floor's
// hot path. The identity census stays there; the READING FIELD of a new row lives here.
//
// THE PROVEN CLASS, STATED SO THE PR DOES NOT RE-DERIVE THE POLICY: witnesses whose observed
// CPU exceeds `required_floor_per_subject_cpu_line_ms` (the 500ms CPU line -- CPU milliseconds, NOT the
// work envelope: they share a magnitude and are different quantities) plus censored
// witnesses that never reached a verdict. A censored reading must ESTABLISH that supplied
// ceiling (censoring_ceiling equals it, lower bound at least it) and the attempt must CARRY
// `FloorCostDebtNeverReachedAVerdict` — censoring is not that discriminator.
// required_floor treats the roster and the long home as ONE declaration class. This constructor
// is what makes "one declaration class" true IN EVIDENCE: a margin crossing (over 302, under
// 500) cannot mint a row, and a 1ms censored reading against the 500ms ceiling cannot either.
//
// THE CEILING IS A PARAMETER. This module must not import `required_floor` (cycle through
// floor_cost_debt) and must not restate 500. Callers pass
// `required_floor_per_subject_cpu_line_ms()`.
//
// DECLARED FRONTIER (DESIGN §3c), not a live mint. `floor_cost_debt_row` is consumed by
// `floor_cost_debt_admit_attempts` and by executing tests; it is NOT consumed by
// `floor_cost_debt_roster`. The live withhold set is still those identity strings. Wiring
// this module into every required-floor compile would import `gunbc.floor_cost_distribution`
// onto that hot path (the reason the constructor is not inside `floor_cost_debt`).
//
// NAMED CONSUMER: `v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin` `enrolment_typed_cost_debt_identities`
// decodes this list onto enrolment Roster ground. The withhold HashSet union into
// `floor_cost_debt_roster` remains a later consumer: the first identity that would otherwise
// be appended as a string after this PR is authored here as a `FloorCostDebtReadingAttempt`
// and nowhere else. Until then this list is Empty, which is the honest population.

// ── THE FIRST INHABITANTS, AND WHY THEY ARE THESE ────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// THE HEADER ABOVE RESERVED THIS LIST for "the first identity that would otherwise be appended as a
// string after this PR", and `v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin` states that its own end-to-end
// execution waits on the first attempt appearing here -- "emptiness of today's list is not coverage".
// These twenty-three are that first population.
//
// WHAT THEY ARE. Every row of `test.claim.spark.relaunch_capture_witness_test` decodes at least one
// 18 KB `docker inspect` document captured verbatim off the Group B serving arm on 2026-09-16. Those
// captures are the only place the container decoder, `relaunch_delta` and `transport_flipped` execute
// over bytes a daemon actually produced, and the socket/RoCE pair is what makes them discriminating
// rather than decorative -- so the cost buys the one thing a designed fixture cannot.
//
// WHY THE COST IS NOT REDUCIBLE, established before it was declared. The figure is the JSON parse of a
// real document and it does not move when the assertions move: a row asserting one field of one
// decoded container costs 533 ms and a row asserting six costs 557 ms, while a row decoding four
// documents costs 2126 ms. Two reductions were made first -- a `witness_holds` conjunction that re-ran
// every row a second time was deleted, and the rows that decoded one document twice now decode it once
// -- and what remains is one decode per document per claim.
//
// WHY NOT THE LONG HOME, which is the other non-blocking ground and looks like the natural answer:
// `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots` carries a blanket `test/claim/long/` exclusion at dir grain that removes
// those entries from per-PR discovery, so relocating would have bought a green floor by making the
// wall execute nowhere. That is DESIGN section 6's inert lens, on the rows that discriminate the
// actuation path of a four-host serving arm.
//
// THE READINGS ARE RE-TAKEN WHENEVER A ROW CHANGES, because a figure carried past the edit that
// invalidated it is a transcription rather than a measurement -- and this list's whole claim is that
// it is the second kind.
//
// EVERY FIGURE IS MEASURED, NOT ESTIMATED, and named by its producer rather than only transcribed:
// `claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry
// dag/test/claim/spark/relaunch_capture_witness_test.dag --functions <the seventeen>` prints
// `[witness] <name>: cpu=<n>ms ... eval_steps=<k>` per row, which is the same reading
// `required-floor-claim-cost` publishes -- cross-checked against run 35150370426, where the four rows
// that survived unrenamed read 2183/2166/529/554 ms there against 2311/2343/596/606 ms here. THE
// SPREAD BETWEEN THE TWO IS THE HOST, not the rows: these readings are taken on a shared session
// container and CI's on a dedicated runner, which is why the class test is `> 500 ms` rather than an
// equality and why every row here clears it by a margin rather than at it.
fn floor_cost_debt_typed_admission_attempts() -> List<FloorCostDebtReadingAttempt> {
  [
    relaunch_capture_reading(
      name: "w_every_captured_inspect_document_decodes",
      cpu_ms: 2311,
      eval_steps: 1591601,
    ),
    relaunch_capture_reading(
      name: "w_the_socket_incarnation_reads_as_missing_the_verbs_shape",
      cpu_ms: 596,
      eval_steps: 394269,
    ),
    relaunch_capture_reading(
      name: "w_the_roce_incarnation_reads_as_carrying_the_verbs_shape",
      cpu_ms: 1186,
      eval_steps: 814184,
    ),
    relaunch_capture_reading(
